<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taj-ul-Masajid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th–20th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Taj-ul-Masajid is a mosque in Bhopal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, one of the largest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan-begum">Shah Jahan Begum</a> began it in the late 19th century, but work stopped after her death in 1901 and it was completed only in the 1980s. Its pink facade, white domes and tall minarets dominate the old city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taj-ul-masajid.jpg" alt="Taj-ul-Masajid" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yann · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taj-ul-Masjid,_Bhopal,_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
